CAT = "auwahControl"; SEG = "HOC"
Q = [
('Under the WHS Regulations, what is the first choice for work that involves a risk of a fall?',
 'Work on the ground or a solid construction', ['Use a harness with a short lanyard', 'Use a ladder with a second person footing it', 'Set up a safety net below the work'],
 'The PCBU must ensure, so far as is reasonably practicable, that work with a fall risk is done on the ground or on a solid construction. This eliminates the fall hazard rather than managing it.'),
('Work cannot be done on the ground or a solid construction. What is the next control to consider?',
 'A fall prevention device', ['A fall arrest system', 'A work positioning system', 'An administrative control'],
 'If the fall risk cannot be eliminated, the PCBU must provide a fall prevention device, such as guardrails or a scaffold, if reasonably practicable. Positioning and arrest systems come after.'),
('A fall prevention device is not reasonably practicable. What comes next in the falls hierarchy?',
 'A work positioning system', ['A fall arrest system', 'A no go area with signs', 'A trained safety observer'],
 'The order is fall prevention device, then work positioning system, then fall arrest system. Administrative controls are used for any risk that remains.'),
('Which falls control is used only when prevention devices and work positioning are not reasonably practicable?',
 'A fall arrest system', ['A perimeter guardrail', 'A restraint technique', 'A scaffold platform'],
 'Fall arrest systems, such as harness systems, nets and catch platforms, stop a fall after it starts. They are used only when higher controls are not reasonably practicable or not fully effective alone.'),
('Which order runs from most to least preferred falls control?',
 'Prevention, positioning, arrest', ['Arrest, positioning, prevention', 'Positioning, prevention, arrest', 'Prevention, arrest, positioning'],
 'After working on the ground or a solid construction, the regulations rank fall prevention devices, then work positioning systems, then fall arrest systems. Each step down relies more on people.'),
('When may administrative controls be the only control for a fall risk?',
 'When no higher control is practicable', ['Whenever the job will take under an hour', 'When workers are experienced', 'When the client prefers it'],
 'Administrative controls such as permits and no go areas must not be used on their own unless higher order controls are not reasonably practicable. They usually support other controls.'),
('One fall control on its own is not enough for a task. What should be done?',
 'Combine control measures', ['Pick the cheapest control', 'Rely on worker care', 'Postpone the work indefinitely'],
 'A combination of controls may be used when a single control is not sufficient. Often the best result comes from, say, a scaffold plus a no go area below.'),
("What makes a floor a 'solid construction' for fall safety?",
 'Strong floor, barriers, safe access', ['Any concrete surface, guarded or not', 'Any floor rated to hold a crane', 'A floor with a non-slip coating only'],
 'A solid construction has a surface able to carry the loads, barriers around its perimeter and openings, an even and readily negotiable surface and gradient, and a safe way in and out.'),
('Which change removes the need to work at height altogether?',
 'Prefabricating on the ground', ['Wearing a harness for the job', 'Using a taller ladder', 'Adding a safety observer'],
 'Building components on the ground and lifting them into place eliminates much of the time spent at height. Elimination is the most effective control.'),
('A painter uses an extension-pole roller from the ground instead of climbing a ladder. Which control is this?',
 'Elimination', ['Fall arrest', 'Administrative control', 'Work positioning'],
 'Doing the task from the ground removes the fall hazard entirely, which is elimination. Long-handled tools and ground-level controls are common examples.'),
('What sets a fall prevention device apart from other falls controls?',
 'No adjustment needed once installed', ['It must be worn by the worker', 'It stops a fall after it has started', 'It relies on signs and permits'],
 'A fall prevention device, once installed, needs no ongoing adjustment, alteration or operation by anyone to keep it working. Guardrails, scaffolds, EWPs and covers are examples.'),
('Which of these is a fall prevention device?',
 'Perimeter guardrail', ['Full body harness', 'Horizontal restraint line', 'Safety net'],
 'Guardrails stop a person reaching the edge without any action by the worker. A restraint line is work positioning, and harnesses and nets are part of fall arrest.'),
('Which of these is a work positioning system?',
 'Industrial rope access', ['Mobile scaffold tower', 'Safety net under the work', 'Catch platform'],
 'Work positioning systems hold a person in position so a fall is prevented. They include the restraint technique and industrial rope access systems.'),
('Which of these is a fall arrest system?',
 'Catch platform', ['Restraint technique', 'Scissor lift', 'Perimeter guardrail'],
 'Catch platforms, safety nets and individual fall arrest systems are designed to stop a fall that has already started and reduce its impact.'),
('Which of these is an administrative control for falls?',
 'A permit system', ['A scaffold bay', 'A roof guardrail', 'A safety net'],
 'Administrative controls are systems of work such as permits, no go areas and sequencing of work. They rely on people following rules, so they rank lowest.'),
('Besides the work area itself, what must the PCBU make safe for work at height?',
 'Access to and exit from it', ['The kitchen in the site office', 'The car park entrance', "The client's meeting room"],
 'The PCBU must provide a safe means of access to and exit from the workplace and any area from which a person could fall, such as a scaffold or platform.'),
('Fall controls are in place. What must be done so they stay effective?',
 'Maintain and inspect them regularly', ['Leave them alone until the job ends', 'Replace them all every single week', 'Check them only after someone falls'],
 'Control measures must be maintained so they remain fit for purpose and are installed, set up and used correctly. A planned inspection and maintenance program does this.'),
('Which event means fall controls must be reviewed?',
 'A change that may add a risk', ['A public holiday falling mid-job', 'The end of a financial year', 'A delivery arriving on time'],
 'Controls must be reviewed when they are not working, before a change that may create a new risk, when a new hazard is found, when consultation shows a need, or when an HSR asks.'),
('In the general hierarchy of control, which is the least effective control?',
 'PPE', ['Engineering', 'Isolation', 'Substitution'],
 'The hierarchy runs from elimination, through substitution, isolation and engineering controls, to administrative controls and finally PPE, which relies most on human behaviour.'),
('In the general hierarchy of control, which ranks above administrative controls?',
 'Engineering controls', ['Personal protective equipment', 'Warning signs', 'Toolbox talks'],
 'Engineering controls such as guardrails and scaffolds act on the hazard itself. Signs and toolbox talks are administrative, and PPE ranks lowest.'),
('Fixing a permanent guardrail around roof plant is which type of control?',
 'An engineering control', ['An administrative control', 'Personal protective equipment', 'A substitution control'],
 'A physical barrier that stops people reaching the edge is an engineering control and a fall prevention device. It works without people having to do anything.'),
('What should mark a no go area at an unguarded edge?',
 'Barriers and clear signs', ['A verbal warning at smoko', 'A note in the site diary', 'A line of chalk on the floor'],
 'No go areas need clear signs and highly visible, securely fixed barriers, plus supervision so unauthorised workers stay out.'),
('How can sequencing work reduce the risk from work at height?',
 "Trades don't work above each other", ['Every trade works at the same time', 'Edge protection goes up after the trades', 'Height work is done at night'],
 'Organising and sequencing work so different trades are not working above or below each other at the same time reduces exposure to falling objects and congested platforms.'),
('Administrative controls are being relied on for a fall risk. What is often also needed?',
 'A high level of supervision', ['A taller ladder for each worker', 'Fewer workers on site', 'Longer lanyards for everyone'],
 'Administrative controls only work if people follow them, so a high level of supervision may be needed to make sure they are adhered to.'),
('Why is a restraint technique preferred over a fall arrest system?',
 'It stops you reaching the edge', ['It is quicker to set up and pack away', 'It lets you work anywhere', 'It needs no anchor point'],
 'A restraint technique prevents the fall from happening, while fall arrest only stops a fall that has started. That is why work positioning ranks above fall arrest.'),
('When should a new penetration in a floor slab be made safe?',
 'Immediately after it is formed', ['At the end of the working day', 'Before the slab is poured', 'When the next trade arrives on site'],
 'Holes, penetrations and openings must be made safe straight away, for example with fixed covers, barricades or embedded mesh, so no one can fall through.'),
('A task at height takes five minutes once a year. Does this mean fall controls can be skipped?',
 'No, it must still be controlled', ['Yes, short tasks are exempt', 'Yes, if a co-worker watches closely', 'Only if it is below 4 metres'],
 'The duty to manage fall risk applies regardless of how brief the task is. Duration and frequency help choose a control, but they do not remove the need for one.'),
('Which control should be considered before a ladder for a full day of ceiling work?',
 'A mobile scaffold', ['A taller stepladder', 'A longer extension ladder', 'A milk crate on a bench'],
 'Ladders are a last option for longer work. A work platform such as a mobile scaffold or scissor lift is a fall prevention device and gives a stable place to work.'),
]
